body:
Thx for reporting, @onlyflix 👍  Nice sleuthing, @skreborn :100:

It is this method (which is indeed called when we click anywhere in `aio-shell` outside of search results or search box):

https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/331989cea357abf9a20088c41a86a077435d17f7/aio/src/app/app.component.ts#L390-L393

We could easily change it like this:

```diff
-this.locationService.setSearch('', { ...this.locationService.search(), search: undefined });
+const oldSearch = this.locationService.search();
+if (oldSearch.search !== undefined) {
+  this.locationService.setSearch('', { ...oldSearch, search: undefined });
+}
```

@onlyflix or @skreborn: Feel free to submit a PR :wink:

Okay I found the reason for this issue. Like @skreborn already said, it is because of the native history API with replaceState. Chromium browser actually have a bug where the `window.history.replaceState()` call loads all favicons again. Refer to [this StackOverflow post](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/36103904/history-pushstate-in-chrome-make-favicon-request) and [this chromium issue](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=131567) for further information.

The StackOverflow post suggest to change the favicons to base64, which I tested. That makes the problem disappear.

@gkalpak With your solution, the favicons still get downloaded whenever I click on the Angular logo in the top left corner.
